      en: "Wat Xieng Mouane is a Buddhist temple in Luang Prabang, Laos, originally built in the 16th century and later renovated. It features classic Lao architectural elements such as a multi-tiered roof and ornate wooden carvings. The temple's murals depict the Jataka tales—stories of Buddha's previous lives—as well as scenes from daily life in Luang Prabang. The temple holds a revered Buddha image known as Phra Chao Xieng Mouane, which is paraded during the annual New Year celebrations. Wat Xieng Mouane remains an active monastery with monks residing on site.",
